    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: rtlamr 0.9.5, an rtl-sdr receiver for Itron ERT compatible smart
meters in the 900 MHz ISM band. Never submitted to Factory before.

Developed in hardware:sdr, where Martin Hauke has maintained it since 2019; I
have added myself to the package _meta as a co-maintainer.

FOR LEGAL REVIEW - the licence tag needs a look:

  License: AGPL-3.0-only AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause

rtlamr's own sources grant &quot;version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any
later version&quot;, so on its own it would be AGPL-3.0-or-later. It is tagged
-only because of a vendored dependency: github.com/bemasher/rtltcp is linked
into the binary, and at the revision go.mod pins it ships NO licence text at
all. That project's repository has since gained a LICENSE holding the bare
AGPLv3 with no or-later grant. So the aggregate cannot be conveyed under a
later AGPL, and -or-later would overstate what recipients get. Whether the
later-added LICENSE covers the pinned revision is a call for legal, not for
me; the reasoning is recorded in a Legal-Review-Notice above the tag.

The rest of the expression: BSD-3-Clause from the in-tree r900/gf package (Go
Authors, imported by r900) and from vendored golang.org/x/xerrors;
BSD-2-Clause from vendored github.com/pkg/errors. All four notices ship under
%license. go.mod also requires sirupsen/logrus, but no source file imports it,
so go mod vendor omits it and it is not linked.

Other review notes:

* rtlamr-no-debug-stdout-print.patch is a backport of upstream commit
  a1f6df82a21f80558c9abfc2b891ee68bb651a57 (&quot;Remove errant fmt.Println.&quot;,
  bemasher, 2026-04-25), not a downstream invention. It sits exactly one
  commit past the v0.9.5 tag and is in no release yet, so 0.9.5 still has the
  bug: init() wrote the compile-time source directory to stdout on every run,
  and stdout is the data channel (the csv/json/xml encoders write there), so
  it corrupted the first line of every machine-readable dump. The patch keeps
  upstream's authorship and the spec comment says to drop it once a release
  contains a1f6df8.

* vendor.tar.gz was regenerated for 0.9.5 with the go_modules source service.
  The vendored module set is identical to the one 0.9.3 shipped.

* The spec moves off the golang-packaging %goprep/%gobuild/%goinstall macros
  to the go-modules idiom from the packaging guidelines. %check added, running
  upstream's test suite.

Built locally on aarch64 for Tumbleweed and Leap 16.0: rpmlint clean, tests
pass, binary runs.</comment>
